-- Work situations, by short names.
`ongoing`      MEANS `in paid work as an ongoing employee or fixed term contractor (s 81)`
`casual short` MEANS `in paid work, casually, with fewer than 260 hours in the 52 weeks before`
`not working, 260 hours` MEANS `not in paid work, but in paid work for at least 260 hours in the 52 weeks before (ss 79 (1) (a), 83)`
`earlier MAI` MEANS `receiving income replacement benefits under this Act for an earlier accident (s 79 (1) (b))`
`unpaid leave` MEANS `on unpaid leave from paid work, expecting to return (ss 79 (1) (c), 85)`
`student`      MEANS `a full-time student expecting paid work after the course or the final year of school (ss 79 (1) (e), 87)`
`IRB` MEANS `income replacement benefits or treatment and care benefits`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Mia, 34, an ongoing employee, is injured on Monday 3 August 2026 and cannot work. She reaches pension age on
-- 10 May 2059. She applies on 20 August 2026. Pre-injury weekly income, AWE adjusted, $1 500; employer super paid; SG
-- 12%; no workers compensation. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 55 (1) (a): the injured person may apply. (2) (b): so may the personal representative. Nobody else here.
#ASSERT `May I apply for defined benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I apply for defined benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply for defined benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 58 (a): 13 weeks beginning Monday 3 August 2026 end on Sunday 1 November 2026 (3 Aug + 90 days).
#ASSERT `By when must I apply` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `1 Nov 2026`
-- s 59 (2) (a) (i): within 2 years after the date of the accident: 3 August 2028.
#ASSERT `What is the last day for a late application` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `3 Aug 2028`
-- s 59 (1): applied 20 August 2026, in the period.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `20 Aug 2026` `20 Aug 2026` `no response yet` `20 Aug 2026` `20 Aug 2026` EQUALS `made within the application period (s 59 (1))`
-- On the last day, 1 November, still in time; on 2 November, late (and no response yet, asked the same day).
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Nov 2026` `1 Nov 2026` `no response yet` `1 Nov 2026` `1 Nov 2026` EQUALS `made within the application period (s 59 (1))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` `no response yet` `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer may accept, if satisfied the applicant has a full and satisfactory explanation (s 59 (2))`

-- s 60 (1): received 20 August; HYPOTHETICAL guideline period of 5 days: 25 August 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me a receipt notice` `20 Aug 2026` 5 EQUALS `25 Aug 2026`
-- s 65 (1): receipt notice 25 August; 28 days after: 22 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer decide liability` `25 Aug 2026` EQUALS `22 Sep 2026`
-- s 65 (1), (4): nothing by 22 September: not yet decided on the 22nd, taken to have accepted on the 23rd.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `no notice given yet` `22 Sep 2026` `22 Sep 2026` EQUALS `not yet decided: the 28 days after the receipt notice have not ended (s 65 (1))`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `no notice given yet` `23 Sep 2026` `23 Sep 2026` EQUALS `taken to have accepted liability: no transfer or rejection notice within 28 days after the receipt notice (s 65 (4))`
-- A rejection notice on 20 September is in time; one on 23 September is too late to stop deemed acceptance.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `a rejection notice: liability not accepted` `20 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `liability rejected (s 65 (3) (b))`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `a rejection notice: liability not accepted` `23 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `taken to have accepted liability: no transfer or rejection notice within 28 days after the receipt notice (s 65 (4))`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `a transfer notice: another insurer is liable` `1 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `liability transferred to another insurer (s 65 (3) (a))`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer accepted liability` `25 Aug 2026` `a defined benefits notice: liability accepted` `1 Sep 2026` `1 Oct 2026` EQUALS `liability accepted (s 65 (2))`

-- s 89: 34, in paid work; no limitation.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
-- s 93: 10 August and 1 November (day 90) are in the first payment period; 2 November is in the second; 3 August 2031
-- (5 years after) is the last day of the second; 4 August 2031 is outside.
#ASSERT `Which payment period is this day in` `3 Aug 2026` `10 Aug 2026` EQUALS `the first payment period (s 93)`
#ASSERT `Which payment period is this day in` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the first payment period (s 93)`
#ASSERT `Which payment period is this day in` `3 Aug 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the second payment period (s 93)`
#ASSERT `Which payment period is this day in` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2031` EQUALS `the second payment period (s 93)`
#ASSERT `Which payment period is this day in` `3 Aug 2026` `4 Aug 2031` EQUALS `outside the payment periods (s 93)`
-- s 101 (3) (a): start on the accident date; (2) (b) (ii): the earlier of 10 May 2061 (pension age + 2 years) and
-- 3 August 2031 (5 years): 3 August 2031.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2031`

-- Mia's week, by the day asked about, her pre-injury income, post-injury capacity, super, SG and workers compensation.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `pre`     IS A NUMBER
      `cap`     IS A NUMBER
      `super`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `sg`      IS A NUMBER
      `wc`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income replacement answer`
`Mia's week of` `the day` `pre` `cap` `super` `sg` `wc` MEANS
    `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `the day` `3 Aug 2026` 34 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` `pre` `cap` `super` `sg` `wc`

-- s 96, 1 September 2026 (1 April 2026 figures): P = 1500 (under $2 794); P >= $1 026, so N = 0.95; 1500 x 0.95 =
-- 1425 a week, 2850 a fortnight.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `1 Sep 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1425 2850
-- s 96, 15 October 2026 (1 October 2026 figures): P >= $1 052, N = 0.95: 1425 a week.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `15 Oct 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1425 2850
-- s 97, 9 November 2026: P = 1500 > $1 279, so N = 0.8; 1500 x 0.8 = 1200 a week, 2400 a fortnight.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `9 Nov 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 1200 2400
-- s 97 with a post-injury earning capacity of $500: (1500 - 500) x 0.8 = 800 a week, 1600 a fortnight. N is set by P,
-- not by P - A.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `9 Nov 2026` 1500 500 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 800 1600
-- s 98: $300 workers compensation for the week: 1425 - 300 = 1125 a week, 2250 a fortnight.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `15 Oct 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 300 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1125 2250
-- 1 April 2027: no deposited biannual figures (the next indexation day): not covered.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `1 Apr 2027` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits not covered` `no deposited AWE indexed amounts for ss 96, 97 and 103 on that day (NI2026-402 covers 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027)`
-- 31 March 2027 is still covered: second period, 1200 a week.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `31 Mar 2027` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 1200 2400
-- 4 August 2031: after the s 101 end date.
#ASSERT `Mia's week of` `4 Aug 2031` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `no income replacement benefits` `the day is outside the period for which income replacement benefits are payable (s 101)`

-- Mia's interim weekly payments (s 103). The insurer asks for information on 17 August 2026. (b) 28 days after:
-- 14 September; (c) 13 weeks after the accident: 2 November. Not given: 14 September. Given on 1 September: 1 September.
#ASSERT `Until when may I get interim weekly payments` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` FALSE `17 Aug 2026` EQUALS `14 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `Until when may I get interim weekly payments` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` TRUE `1 Sep 2026` EQUALS `1 Sep 2026`
-- Asked on 20 October: 28 days after is 17 November, but 13 weeks after the accident is 2 November: 2 November.
#ASSERT `Until when may I get interim weekly payments` `3 Aug 2026` `20 Oct 2026` FALSE `20 Oct 2026` EQUALS `2 Nov 2026`
-- s 103 (3), HYPOTHETICAL prescribed percentage 80: on 20 August 2026 (1 April 2026 figures), 80% of $2 794 = 2235.20.
#ASSERT `How much interim weekly payment may the insurer pay me` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` FALSE `17 Aug 2026` 80 `20 Aug 2026` EQUALS `dollars` 2235.2
-- On 15 September the period has ended (it ended on 14 September).
#ASSERT `How much interim weekly payment may the insurer pay me` `3 Aug 2026` `17 Aug 2026` FALSE `17 Aug 2026` 80 `15 Sep 2026` EQUALS `nothing payable` `the interim weekly payment period has ended (s 103 (2))`

-- Treatment and care (s 112, s 128): entitled; from the accident to 5 years after.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to treatment and care benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `When are my treatment and care benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` `20 Aug 2026` FALSE EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2031`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. The s 96 example ("Kristin"), with today's figures. A part-time teacher's assistant, pre-injury income $700
-- a week, employer super paid; injured 1 October 2026; applies the same day. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `pre`     IS A NUMBER
      `super`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `sg`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income replacement answer`
`a week from 1 October 2026, on` `the day` `pre` `super` `sg` MEANS
    `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `the day` `1 Oct 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` `pre` 0 `super` `sg` 0

-- s 96: $175 < 700 < $1 052, so N = 1 + SG/100. With the example's SG of 9.5: 700 x 1.095 = 766.50 (the example's own
-- figure); fortnight 1533.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 700 TRUE 9.5 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 766.5 1533
-- With SG 12 (2025-26 on): 700 x 1.12 = 784; fortnight 1568.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 700 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 784 1568
-- s 96 (2) (b): no employer super, SG = 0, N = 1.0: 700.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 700 FALSE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 700 1400
-- s 96 (1) N (a): P at or under $175, N = 1.0: 150 gives 150; 175 gives 175; 176 gives 176 x 1.12 = 197.12.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 150 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 150 300
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 175 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 175 350
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 176 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 197.12 394.24

-- FINDING 1 (the cliffs). N applies to the whole of (P - A). First period: P = 1051, N = 1.12: 1177.12; P = 1052,
-- N = 0.95: 999.40. One dollar more of pre-injury income costs $177.72 a week.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 1051 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1177.12 2354.24
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 1052 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 999.4 1998.8
-- Second period (4 January 2027; the first ended 30 December 2026): P = 1279, N = 0.95: 1215.05; P = 1280, N = 0.8:
-- 1024. One dollar more costs $191.05 a week.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `4 Jan 2027` 1279 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 1215.05 2430.1
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `4 Jan 2027` 1280 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 1024 2048
-- The P cap ($2 864): pre-injury income $3 000. First period 2864 x 0.95 = 2720.80; second 2864 x 0.8 = 2291.20.
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `5 Oct 2026` 3000 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 2720.8 5441.6
#ASSERT `a week from 1 October 2026, on` `4 Jan 2027` 3000 TRUE 12 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the second payment period (s 93)` 2291.2 4582.4

-- FINDING 5. Post-injury earning capacity above pre-injury income: P = 600, A = 700. (600 - 700) x 1.12 is negative;
-- read as nil.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `5 Oct 2026` `1 Oct 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` 600 700 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 0 0
-- A capped P with capacity: (2864 - 500) x 0.95 = 2245.80.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `5 Oct 2026` `1 Oct 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE `1 Oct 2026` 3000 500 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 2245.8 4491.6

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. Indexation day moves N. Injured 15 July 2026 (first period to 13 October 2026), pre-injury income $1 040,
-- super paid, SG 12. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- 1 September 2026 (1 April 2026 figures): 1040 >= $1 026, N = 0.95: 988. 1 October 2026: 1040 < $1 052, N = 1.12:
-- 1164.80. The weekly amount rises by $176.80 on the indexation day.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `1 Sep 2026` `15 Jul 2026` 30 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Jul 2026` FALSE `15 Jul 2026` 1040 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 988 1976
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `1 Oct 2026` `15 Jul 2026` 30 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Jul 2026` FALSE `15 Jul 2026` 1040 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits` `the first payment period (s 93)` 1164.8 2329.6
-- Before 1 April 2026 there are no deposited figures: injured 2 March 2026, asked about 10 March 2026: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `10 Mar 2026` `2 Mar 2026` 30 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Mar 2026` FALSE `2 Mar 2026` 1040 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits not covered` `no deposited AWE indexed amounts for ss 96, 97 and 103 on that day (NI2026-402 covers 1 April 2026 to 31 March 2027)`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. Entitlement (ss 89-92, 43-50). Injured 3 August 2026 unless said. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 89 (1) (a): 14 on the date of the accident.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 14 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `under 15 on the date of the motor accident (s 89 (1) (a))`
-- s 89 (1) (b): neither in paid work nor capable of it.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `none of these` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `neither in paid work nor capable of being in paid work on the date of the motor accident (ss 78, 79, 89 (1) (b))`
-- s 79 (1) (a): not working but 260 hours in the year before: capable, so entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `not working, 260 hours` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
-- s 90: pension age reached on 1 January 2026; not in paid work (only capable): not entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 67 `not working, 260 hours` `1 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `pension age reached and not in paid work on the date of the motor accident (s 90)`
-- s 90: pension-aged and in paid work: entitled, and s 101 (2) (b) (i) ends the period 2 years after the accident.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 67 `ongoing` `1 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 67 `ongoing` `1 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2028`
-- s 101 (2) (b) (ii): reaching pension age on 1 January 2028, 2 years later is 1 January 2030, before 3 August 2031.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 65 `ongoing` `1 Jan 2028` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Jan 2030`
-- s 92: damages for loss of income already paid.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `an insurer has already paid damages for loss of income (s 92)`
-- s 48: a serious offence; s 47: a detainee; s 50: workers compensation accepted; s 43 (2): uninsured, no exception.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `a limitation in division 2.2.2 ends or excludes these benefits (ss 43 to 50)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `a limitation in division 2.2.2 ends or excludes these benefits (ss 43 to 50)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not entitled` `a limitation in division 2.2.2 ends or excludes these benefits (ss 43 to 50)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `a limitation in division 2.2.2 ends or excludes these benefits (ss 43 to 50)`

-- Which limitation bears on which benefit (the "subject to" lists), on the core. One driving offence (s 44) ends
-- income replacement and quality of life benefits but not treatment and care (s 112 (2) does not list s 44).
`only s 44` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes income replacement benefits` `only s 44`
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes quality of life benefits` `only s 44`
#ASSERT NOT (`division 2.2.2 ends or excludes treatment and care benefits` `only s 44`)
-- s 47 (a detainee): income replacement and treatment and care, not quality of life (s 132 (2) does not list s 47).
`only s 47` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes income replacement benefits` `only s 47`
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes treatment and care benefits` `only s 47`
#ASSERT NOT (`division 2.2.2 ends or excludes quality of life benefits` `only s 47`)
-- s 43 (3) bears only on quality of life benefits; s 43 (2) only on income replacement benefits.
`only s 43 (3)` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`division 2.2.2 ends or excludes income replacement benefits` `only s 43 (3)`)
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes quality of life benefits` `only s 43 (3)`
`only s 43 (2)` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes income replacement benefits` `only s 43 (2)`
#ASSERT NOT (`division 2.2.2 ends or excludes quality of life benefits` `only s 43 (2)`)
-- s 46 (self-inflicted): income replacement and quality of life, not treatment and care.
`only s 46` MEANS `my division 2.2.2 facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`division 2.2.2 ends or excludes treatment and care benefits` `only s 46`)
#ASSERT `division 2.2.2 ends or excludes quality of life benefits` `only s 46`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. When payments start (s 101 (3)-(5)), and two work situations s 101 does not provide for. Injured 3 August
-- 2026, application period ending 1 November 2026. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 101 (3) (b) (i): an ongoing employee applies late on 1 December 2026: 28 days before is 3 November 2026.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
-- (3) (b) (ii): with exceptional circumstances, from the accident.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `ongoing` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` TRUE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
-- s 101 (4) (a): on unpaid leave, expecting to return 1 September 2026, applying in time: from 1 September.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `unpaid leave` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `1 Sep 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
-- (4) (b) (i): late on 1 December: the later of 1 September and 3 November: 3 November.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `unpaid leave` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` FALSE `1 Sep 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
-- Expecting to return on 15 November: the later of 15 November and 3 November: 15 November.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `unpaid leave` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Dec 2026` FALSE `15 Nov 2026` EQUALS `payable from and to` `15 Nov 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
-- s 101 (5) (a): a full-time student, 19, expecting to start work on 1 February 2027, applying in time: from then.
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 19 `student` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `1 Feb 2027` EQUALS `payable from and to` `1 Feb 2027` `3 Aug 2031`
-- On unpaid leave until 1 September, a week in August is before the start date.
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `20 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `unpaid leave` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `1 Sep 2026` 1500 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `no income replacement benefits` `the day is outside the period for which income replacement benefits are payable (s 101)`
-- FINDING 3. In casual paid work with fewer than 260 hours: in paid work (s 78), so entitled (s 89), but no s 101
-- start date (and no s 81-87 pre-injury income): not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 20 `casual short` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 20 `casual short` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `period not covered` `no start date in s 101 (3) to (5) for this work situation`
#ASSERT `How much income replacement benefit do I get` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2026` 20 `casual short` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` 400 0 TRUE 12 0 EQUALS `income replacement benefits not covered` `no start date in s 101 (3) to (5) for this work situation`
-- FINDING 4. Receiving income replacement benefits for an earlier accident: capable (s 79 (1) (b)), entitled, no start
-- date.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to income replacement benefits` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `earlier MAI` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `When are my income replacement benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` 40 `earlier MAI` `10 May 2059` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Aug 2026` FALSE `3 Aug 2026` EQUALS `period not covered` `no start date in s 101 (3) to (5) for this work situation`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 6. Late applications (s 59). Injured 3 August 2026; applies late on 1 December 2026, the insurer receiving the
-- explanation the same day (28 days after: 29 December 2026). HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

`29 Dec 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 29 12 2026
`30 Dec 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 12 2026
`21 Dec 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 21 12 2026
`11 Dec 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 11 12 2026

-- s 59 (2): asked about on 11 December, no response yet: the insurer may accept, if satisfied.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `11 Dec 2026` `11 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer may accept, if satisfied the applicant has a full and satisfactory explanation (s 59 (2))`
-- s 59 (4): still no response on 30 December: taken to have accepted. On 29 December (day 28), not yet.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `30 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer is taken to have accepted: no response to the explanation within 28 days (s 59 (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `no response yet` `29 Dec 2026` `29 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer may accept, if satisfied the applicant has a full and satisfactory explanation (s 59 (2))`
-- Accepted, or refused, on 21 December: in time.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `accepted the late application` `21 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer has accepted (s 59 (2))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `refused the late application` `21 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer has refused (s 59 (2))`
-- Refused on 30 December, day 29: too late; already taken to have accepted.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `1 Dec 2026` `refused the late application` `30 Dec 2026` `30 Dec 2026` EQUALS `a late application the insurer is taken to have accepted: no response to the explanation within 28 days (s 59 (4))`
-- s 59 (5): applied on 4 August 2028, after the 2-year limit (3 August 2028); silence does not accept it (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `4 Aug 2028` `4 Aug 2028` `no response yet` `4 Aug 2028` `1 Oct 2027` EQUALS `made after the late application limit: the insurer need not accept it (s 59 (5))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `IRB` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2028` `3 Aug 2028` `no response yet` `3 Aug 2028` `3 Aug 2028` EQUALS `a late application the insurer may accept, if satisfied the applicant has a full and satisfactory explanation (s 59 (2))`
-- s 128 (2) (a) (ii): a late application on 1 December, no exceptional circumstances: treatment and care from 13 weeks
-- before, 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `When are my treatment and care benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` FALSE EQUALS `payable from and to` `1 Sep 2026` `3 Aug 2031`
#ASSERT `When are my treatment and care benefits payable` `3 Aug 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE EQUALS `payable from and to` `3 Aug 2026` `3 Aug 2031`

